WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.270
Here in this school, we'll use these five machines.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.720
We'll have two people to a car, taking turns driving.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.960
Please confirm the car number and whether you'll be in group A or B.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.420
Now we will have each one of you introduce yourselves.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.850
Please give us your name, age, and karting experience.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:20.420
First, A-kun.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.280
Car #1, Taira-kun.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.380
Y-Yes.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.100
I'm first?!

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.690
U-Umm, good morning.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.660
Taira Capeta.  I'm 15 years old.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.100
I've been driving karts for five years.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:18.120
Last year I took the Japan National Junior title, and this year I'm racing in the East ICA class.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.290
I didn't expect to drive in a formula car, so I'm really nervous.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.040
<i>That's right, Tanaka-san.</i>

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.570
<i>He's Taira.</i>

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.510
<i>Please take good care of Taira.</i>

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.290
I'll do my best.  It's a pleasure working with all of you.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.740
Next, Shiba-kun.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.680
Yes.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.710
H-Hi.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.540
Shiba Ryou.  I'm 16 years old.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.530
I've been karting for six years.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.240
I came in 4th place last year in the East Japan National ICA class.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.200
I'm currently the point leader this season.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.500
I came here to win the scholarship!

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.280
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.120
<i>That Shiba...</i>

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.710
<i>We let you win last time,
 but it won't be like that this time.</i>

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.370
<i>That scholarship is ours!</i>

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.680
<i>We won't let you have it!</i>

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.640
<i>But what's the point in me getting all worked up.</i>

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.560
<i>You also think so, right Cape—</i>

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.430
<i>Hey!</i>

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.630
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.230
<i>Be more stern!</i>

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.520
<i>The battle's started!</i>

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.800
Hata Noriko.  I'm 17 years old.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.390
I come from Nagoya.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:31.860
I've been karting for 12 years and came in 3rd in the M4 series last year.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.010
I've also won a race this year.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.610
So that's Hata-san's daughter.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.870
She's quite pretty.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.740
I'll do my best.  It's a pleasure working with you all.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:46.660
<i>So she's the daughter of Hata,
an ex-driver in the Japan National F3000.</i>

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.280
<i>She was in the magazine.</i>

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.260
<i>Apparently she's quite fast,</i>

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.050
<i>and I bet she practiced a lot on a formula car prior to this through her father's connections.</i>

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.550
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.720
<i>If you let your guard down you'll be beaten, Capeta...</i>

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.680
<i>C-Capeta?!</i>

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.820
<i>You...!  That's the enemy!</i>

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.190
<i>This is bad.  She's totally his type!</i>

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.010
I come from Fukuoka.  The name is Daiki Souta.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.160
I'm 18 years old.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.740
I have seven years experience in karting.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.030
I've started racing in the FJ this year.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.200
I applied because I want the scholarship.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.030
I'll do my best.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.730
Isa Hiroshi.  I'm 17 years old.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.260
I come from Shiga.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.850
I'm in the top ranking this year in the West M4 series.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:24.620
Please give me a lot of advice.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.810
<i>Since they're all in group A,
he'll be racing against them on the final day.</i>

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.340
<i>This is tough.</i>

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.800
<i>They're all famous.</i>

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.640
Who's that pretty girl?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.430
Some driver's sister?

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.740
No, probably his girlfriend.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.730
That's so annoying.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.880
Monami-chan, what are you doing?

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.810
Exercising.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.830
Huh?!  In this hot weather?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.220
I'm on a diet right now so it's convenient.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.550
Why a diet?

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.200
You're thin enough.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.580
I was told that I should lose 5 kg
 if I wanted to be a model.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.420
And they said my breasts are too big.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.210
What a waste!

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.380
They're going to get smaller?!

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.670
I'd be eating a lot of stuff if I was back home, so this is convenient.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.340
I'll lose 3 kg during these three days.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.550
So that's why you came with us.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.560
By the way, I wonder what Ca-chan is doing at the briefing.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:26.820
It says something about the structure of the machine here.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.960
Ca-chan seems to be weak at those types of things.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.030
I wonder if he'll understand everything.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.870
Well, my name is Shinkawa.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.820
Nice to meet you.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.540
<i>So this person is Shinkawa.</i>

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.540
<i>A Formula Nippon driver.</i>

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.250
Before I start the lecture,
let me tell you something useful.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:53.250
This place is called
 "Formula Stellar Racing School," but...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.720
that's just a name President Kagami came up with.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.550
It's not a school at all.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.970
Don't be fooled.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:00.680
<i>Shinkawa!</i>

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:06.930
Of course, we'll teach you all about the machine and racing during this three-day course.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:12.900
However, it's not our intention to turn you all into full-fledged racing drivers by teaching you everything.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.300
We have no intention of training you.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.800
We're doing this to find you.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.030
So be sure that all of you understand.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.030
<i>Shinkawa!</i>

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.720
How is it?

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:41.930
Can you step on it?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:42.750
Yes.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:46.730
How is it?

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.430
Can you grip it easily?

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.500
Yes.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.440
I'm okay.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.470
All right, here are some pointers on adjusting the seat.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.110
The car is bigger and the tires are spaced farther apart compared to a kart, aren't they?

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:03.830
That's why a lot of senses don't convey to your body.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:08.940
In order for them to get through to you, it's best 
 to have as much contact between you and the car.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:12.290
Yeah...  I think this is okay.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.750
Hey, you have space by the knees.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.520
If you don't have them tightly touching both sides of the bulk head,

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.500
you won't be able to sense the roll on the sides.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.080
Hey.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.210
Bring me a mat.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:26.970
Okay.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.460
Try putting on full brakes.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.410
Step on the pedal.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.160
Harder.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.330
O-Okay.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.110
Are you lifting at the hips?

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:39.100
If you're lifting, you delay sensing the front and back weight.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.910
Hey.  Two more mats.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:41.570
Okay.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.660
<i>I-It's tight.</i>

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.100
That's how it should be.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:51.250
It lowers your senses if it's even the slightest bit loose.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:54.210
And that's where you get differences in your time.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.690
It doesn't matter if it's comfortable or not, unless it's really painful.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.550
<i>Th-They said tight, but I didn't think they meant this tight.</i>

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.420
<i>I-I can't move.</i>

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.680
<i>I'm already feeling dizzy.</i>

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:08.140
<i>So this is the Formula.</i>

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.900
This is a historical moment.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.010
Taira Capeta finally makes his first step towards the F1!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.110
By the great manager, Andou Nobu.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.560
Who's a great manager?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.850
You're like a stalker secretly taking pictures.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:29.080
I told you I'm doing this because I didn't want to bother the professional instructors or mechanics.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.450
He sure is blessed.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:35.380
Being instructed by all those professional adults.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:39.260
On top of that, the instructor for car #1 is Shinkawa.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.460
He's really lucky.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.370
We've paid 210,000 yen after all.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.470
And I donated 20,000 yen, too.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.430
She sure is persistent about that.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.250
Okay.  Everyone pay attention!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.060
Everyone in group A,
 you're all done adjusting your seats, right?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.770
Anyone who hasn't shifted gears or handled a clutch before,

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.440
or who's not confident, please gather over here.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.300
We will practice on that car over there with an instructor.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.200
Anyone who is worried, please say so.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.700
I'm fine.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.160
Me, too.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.580
<i>They've all practiced.</i>

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.080
<i>I... should practice.</i>

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:18.080
All right, we're gonna practice while group B adjusts their seats, so hurry up!

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:19.790
Nobu!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.260
Nobu!

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:27.720
Didn't you say it's much better risking it on the spot, rather than getting used to something similar?!

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.400
No, um, that's...

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.900
What was it?!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.680
They're practicing on a normal car after all!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.440
I thought you were cool back then, but we really can't rely on you.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.150
You're disqualified from being the manager.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.020
Poor Ca-chan.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.840
C-Capeta!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.000
Capeta!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.740
I'm sorry!

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:00.410
Okay.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.290
Have a look at this.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:03.500
You see, there are three pedals.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.710
Yes.

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:07.910
The kart only has the accelerator and brake,

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.720
but there are three pedals on this car and on the formula car you're going to be driving.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.070
The one on the left is the clutch.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:16.640
You step on this when you change gears.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.700
<i>He's good.</i>

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.000
Now try stepping on it.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.930
As far as you can with your left foot.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.410
Okay.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.430
The gear is set to neutral right now.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.760
While stepping on the clutch, put it in 1.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:46.050
While stepping on the accelerator with your right foot,
 slowly open the clutch with your left.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:52.410
Don't rush it.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.570
Make sure to do it step by step.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.340
Yes.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.480
<i>He can't even start properly?!</i>

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.450
<i>It's my turn next.</i>

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.120
Okay.  One more time.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:16.360
You're not getting the engine revolutions right.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.650
I'm sorry.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.370
C-Capeta...

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:23.830
Mom!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.840
Lunch is ready.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:26.800
Mom!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.920
I know.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.800
I heard you.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.790
By the way, doesn't the FSte audition start today?

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.610
It's so hot.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:40.810
It was really tough when you had yours last year.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.530
In October you'll be 16.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.480
You'll finally get a restricted A license.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.670
Yeah.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.870
I got a call from the team yesterday

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:56.230
and they said they'll prepare a 3rd machine for the 10th race in October and that I should enter.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.850
Sorry, Capeta.  I...

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.230
It's okay, Nobu.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:04.640
It was me who decided in the end after all.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.880
You believed Nobu's irresponsible words in the end, right?

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:08.840
Me too, though.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.040
<i>Oh?</i>

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:11.950
<i>He's here with his girlfriend?</i>

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.260
<i>And his standards are high!</i>

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:17.740
Hey.  Aren't you eating anything, Monami?

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:19.270
This Viking lunch is great.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:20.650
Don't worry about me.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.730
I'm on a diet, so this is enough.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:25.630
<i>I was naive.</i>

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:29.900
<i>In this world, my lukewarm assumptions won't cut it.</i>

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.180
<i>I'll have to do my best from now on.</i>

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.370
<i>Monami-chan is nice.</i>

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.330
<i>Taira...</i>

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.320
<i>we're finally going on the FSte this afternoon.</i>

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.330
<i>I'll kick you off and take the lead!</i>

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:17.210
We'll have you all drive for the first time here...

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.830
but the first thing we'll have you do is a pylon run.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:23.260
Because we're in low gear, you have two aero parts attached.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:27.840
You will hold it in first gear with the engine at 3000 rpm.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:32.210
If you go over the set limit,
 the warning lamp will light up to let us know.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.260
Please be careful.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.350
Can you hear me?

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.370
How do you feel?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.560
<b>Y-Yes.</b>

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.010
<b>I'm okay.</b>

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.440
Great.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:42.870
The aim of this session is to get to know the machine.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:47.480
Like how far to turn the wheel in order to turn the car, and how the brake and accelerator work.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.900
Concentrate on feeling the machine.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:51.480
<b>Okay.</b>

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.810
<i>It's finally time!</i>

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.930
<i>He's going to drive!</i>

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.150
<i>Capeta is going to drive a formula car!</i>

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.490
Okay.  Car #1, start!

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:04.450
<i>Clutch...</i>

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:05.910
<i>Put it in first gear.</i>

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.370
<i>Pump the accelerator.</i>

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.330
<i>All right, I'm going to connect the clutch!</i>

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.290
<i>Go, Capeta!</i>

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.360
What happened?

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.930
The engine stopped.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:26.270
The engine revs decreased when you let go of the clutch.

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:27.670
Pump it up more.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:28.690
<b>Okay.</b>

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:29.500
<i>Don't get hasty.</i>

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:30.440
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:35.530
Okay, start.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.740
He stopped again?

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:42.710
Hey, why can't Ca-chan start?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.890
It's hard to connect the clutch.

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:47.450
It's his first time and it's also a racing clutch.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:51.170
If the 2nd car can go, go ahead.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.250
The car after him started okay.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.430
Damn Shiba.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.980
<b>Car #3, start.</b>

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:11.400
Listen.  Get the timing right for both pumping the accel and releasing the clutch.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.490
Don't worry.

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:17.580
One more time.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.320
Another one went.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.450
<b>What's wrong, car #1 and #5?</b>

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.240
<i>G-Go!</i>

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.000
<i>A little more!</i>

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.220
<i>It's running!</i>

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.170
He did it!

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:35.600
He's going!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.060
Tanaka-san!

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:50.000
Oh, Andou-kun.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.090
Thank you very much.

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.230
That's okay.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:55.980
Taira-kun had a hard time starting, I see.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.690
He didn't practice beforehand, did he?

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:04.060
Umm, will this count as a big demerit against us from the start?

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.250
Not really.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:10.410
Sometimes we have the slowest driver passing the audition.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.620
Shinkawa was like that, too.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.750
<i>That</i> Shinkawa?!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.540
But can you still pass?

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.840
Yeah, because that's not what we're looking for.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.050
Th-Then, what are you looking for?

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.760
I think what we're looking for the most is the level of absorption.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:31.300
Not your current driving speed or how good you are.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:36.870
The one who gets selected is usually the one who grows the most over the three days.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:41.280
In the end, it's those drivers who succeed in professional racing.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.700
<i>Growth rate, huh?</i>

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:48.150
Well, it doesn't matter how badly you drive at first.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.450
Anyway, whatever you do, don't crash, okay?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.440
Don't crash.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.920
H-He won't crash.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.630
<i>He sure is persistent.</i>

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.170
<i>I won't lose...</i>

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.780
<i>And it's not just Taira.</i>

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.950
<i>I'm going to stand on top of the pack!</i>

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.150
<i>He's getting too hot.</i>

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:43.210
<i>He's so dangerous I can't stand watching him.</i>

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:48.390
<i>The back seems to be used to it, though.</i>

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:03.950
<i>My body is strapped in tight, but that doesn't matter anymore once you start driving.</i>

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:06.240
<i>So that's how a formula car is.</i>

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:23.920
<i>It must be extremely fun if you raise the gear and drive faster.</i>

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:37.600
<i>In any case...</i>

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:39.520
<i>Damn!</i>

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:40.800
<i>Why was my start so...?!</i>

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.350
<i>I have to do better.</i>

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.480
<i>I want to race in this machine.</i>

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.210
<i>I want to pass!</i>

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.860
<i>In order to do so, I have to...!</i>

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:01.960
This lesson concludes the first day of the program.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.610
Good job, everyone.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:05.280
Thank you very much.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.600
Well done, Capeta.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.890
Nobu, I did it on the first day!

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:14.100
You idiot, you'll be fine!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.370
I heard just now.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:21.990
FSRS passes the person who's grown the most at the end.

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.570
And apparently Shinkawa was like you in the beginning.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:26.730
Really?!

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:27.880
Yeah.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.490
So if you do your best tomorrow, you'll have no problem whatsoever.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:33.700
Maybe it's a good thing that you messed up on the first day.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:38.550
If you get better from now on, your growth may be noticed the most and it may put you at an advantage.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.170
Not that it's much of an advantage...

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:42.670
I-I see... Yeah!

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.180
Monami, you say good things.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:47.320
That's right.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.290
<i>I-Is it?</i>

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.590
<i>Sometimes I can't follow these two.</i>

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:53.500
Nobu.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:57.410
Today I thought the Formula might be fun.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.560
And I wanted to race in it.

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:02.490
I'll give it all I got!

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:03.840
I'm feeling better now!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:04.930
<i>You're so slow!</i>

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.770
<i>The first day is over!</i>

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.860
It's like coming to see your child's classes in school.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.630
It sure is.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:11.740
<i>Okay.  I'll do it tomorrow!</i>

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:14.700
You're Taira-kun, right?

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.990
Hey, can I tell you something?

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:20.580
I don't think it's right coming here to play around.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.470
W-What are you talking about?

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.110
I'm not playing around!

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.870
That's big talk for someone who brought his girlfriend along.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.880
It lowers my motivation.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.590
She's not my girlfriend!

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:31.860
Then why is she here?!

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.190
She's staying here to diet!

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:35.360
D-Di...

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.100
Huh?  What are you talking about?!

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:39.400
Nobu is my partner.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.060
We're both totally serious!

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:43.100
I won't lose to the likes of you!

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.490
What?!

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.380
I won't lose either!

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:50.400
<i>I'll succeed at the start tomorrow no matter what!</i>

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:51.740
<i>I have to hurry back to image training!</i>

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.220
<i>What?</i>

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:56.370
<i>He must be big-headed because the magazine covered him.</i>

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:57.450
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.610
What's with her?

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.840
What an attitude.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.410
Youth.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.800
Indeed.

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:52.690
Taira sure is enthusiastic.

00:22:52.690 --> 00:22:54.570
Image training before sleeping, huh?

00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:55.900
Oh yeah.

00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:58.620
I just got 30.89 seconds.

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.740
I'll beat you by a wide margin this time.

00:23:00.740 --> 00:23:01.600
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:02.530
Shift Up!

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:05.260
Now's the time to break the limit!
